\lispPackageChapter{livermore/tmscs}

The \texttt{livermore/tmscs} package is the time series classifier
(\textsc{Tsc}) of~\cite{gore-2008}, later named \textsc{Tmscs} when the
representation was allowed more than one series.  It is XCSR whose alleles are
paths through a time series rather than intervals on a single real.
Situations are time series or time multiseries as defined in
$\Sigma$~\cite{gore-sigma}.

A rule is a collection of predicates; each predicate must match the current
situation for the rule to match~\cite{gore-2008}.  A single predicate consists
of an initial and a final position, a field selector $\phi$, an operator
$\omega$, and a range $[l,u]$.  Taking the data along the straight line
segment from the initial point to the final point forms a vector $d$; applying
$\phi$ to each element yields $d'$.  The predicate matches if and only if
$l \le \omega(d') \le u$.  When all of the predicates of the rule match, the
rule recommends a particular classification or action.

\section{Classes}

\lispClassSubsection{tms-predicate}

A subclass of \texttt{range-predicate}.

\begin{description}
\item[\texttt{initial}] The start of the path: temporal index first, then
  array coordinates.
\item[\texttt{final}] The end of the path, in the same form.
\item[\texttt{field}] A function applied to each cell, default
  \texttt{identity}.
\item[\texttt{operation}] A function applied to the sequence of field
  values, default \texttt{identity}.
\end{description}

\texttt{tms-predicate} is also a constructor that applies
\texttt{make-instance}.

\lispClassSubsection{tms-classifier}

A classifier whose condition is a list of \texttt{tms-predicate}s.  It
matches a situation when every predicate matches.

\lispClassSubsection{tmscs-learning-parameters}

A subclass of \texttt{xcsr-learning-parameters}.

\begin{description}
\item[\texttt{maximum-environment-condition-length}] How many predicates a
  covering classifier may have.  Default $1$.
\item[\texttt{maximum-temporal-mutation}] The largest random change to the
  temporal coordinate.  Default $5$.
\item[\texttt{maximum-position-mutation}] The largest random change to any
  spatial coordinate.  Default $5$.
\item[\texttt{valid-operations}] The operations covering and mutation may
  choose.
\item[\texttt{valid-fields}] The fields they may choose.  Default
  \texttt{(list \#'identity)}.
\item[\texttt{visible-time-range}] The window of history the classifiers
  may see.  Default \texttt{(0 100)}.
\end{description}

\lispClassSubsection{tmscs}

An XCSR whose predicate type is \texttt{tms-predicate} and whose classifier
type is \texttt{tms-classifier}.

\section{Methods}

\texttt{path} is the raster line from \texttt{initial} to \texttt{final}.
\texttt{field-path} is the field applied to each cell on that path.
\texttt{operate} applies the operation to that sequence.

\texttt{match?} is true when the operated value lies in the range.
\texttt{more-general?} is true when the ranges and paths nest strictly.

\texttt{cover} picks random endpoints in the visible window, a random field
and operation, and a range around the operated value.

\texttt{mutate} may slide the path a little along its line and move the
bounds, keeping the current situation classified as before.

\texttt{crossover} is one-point on the list of predicates, and may also
swap a prefix of slots inside the predicate at the cut.

\texttt{covering-score} is the path length times the range width as a
fraction of the problem range.
